# File: tests/features/add_greeting_rot13_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/215-add-greeting-rot13-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Apply ROT13 to the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the ROT13 form of the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_rot13 is called with Ada
    Then the result is the Python str Uryyb, Nqn

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Rotate only ASCII letters and leave every other character unchanged
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_rot13 is called with Mary-Jane O'Neil, with Zo followed by precomposed U+00EB, and with fullwidth U+FF3A followed by ed 42
    Then the results are Uryyb, Znel-Wnar B'Arvy and Uryyb, Mb followed by U+00EB and Uryyb, followed by U+FF3A and rq 42
    And every character that is not an ASCII letter is unchanged at the same position

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Applying ROT13 twice restores the greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When ROT13 is applied again to greeting_rot13 of Ada, Zo followed by U+00EB, and Mary-Jane O'Neil
    Then each result equals greet of the same name

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_rot13 is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing existing surfaces
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_rot13 of Ada, and nmg-smoke Ada runs
    Then the example prints Uryyb, Nqn
    And greeting_rot13 is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__ alongside every previously listed export
    And nmg-smoke prints Hello, Ada with one newline and exit status 0
    And the README documents ASCII-only ROT13 of the complete greeting, unchanged other characters, and the inherited invalid-name error
